& =[\\begin{aligned}23 & -18 \\\\ 9 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${H}^{3}={H}^{2}\\cdot H,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{3} & ={H}^{2}\\cdot H \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}23 & -18 \\\\ 9 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}97 & -118 \\\\ 59 & 38\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343723 13194139535323 true] [17592186343722 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535323 true] [17592186343722 1041 "field-1" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343722 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343723 13194139535323 true] [17592186343722 1110 #uuid "2511b505-7340-521c-8ac6-22e68f230d06" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343723 1034 "97" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535323 true] [17592186343723 1111 #uuid "836392e0-9c61-5af5-b537-1d1956bc2624" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343725 13194139535323 true] [17592186343724 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535323 true] [17592186343724 1041 "field-2" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343724 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343725 13194139535323 true] [17592186343724 1110 #uuid "089c19c4-90bb-5e5b-877d-ea9fb78b065e" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343725 1034 "-118" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535323 true] [17592186343725 1111 #uuid "bd439727-a89f-5011-8022-234538a782bb" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343726 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343727 13194139535323 true] [17592186343726 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535323 true] [17592186343726 1041 "field-3" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343726 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343727 13194139535323 true] [17592186343726 1110 #uuid "bde38d0a-ed99-5cd8-aad0-6e4a79f2944b" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343727 1034 "59" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535323 true] [17592186343727 1111 #uuid "64395931-9062-5802-aaf6-d529cefdaddb" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343729 13194139535323 true] [17592186343728 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535323 true] [17592186343728 1041 "field-4" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343728 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343729 13194139535323 true] [17592186343728 1110 #uuid "709c9dfd-3c35-5887-8504-55c653b794b3" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343729 1034 "38" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535323 true] [17592186343729 1111 #uuid "279a4b72-f9ce-50ac-b2ac-593bbb501a05" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343730 1017 #edb/ref 17592186343731 13194139535323 true] [17592186343730 1017 #edb/ref 17592186343734 13194139535323 true] [17592186343730 1089 "q-338763" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343730 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535323 true] [17592186343730 1100 "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions to the equation $-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=7+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343730 1113 #uuid "190ea00f-cebd-5a8c-93af-4aa5ffc827ba" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343730 1142 true 13194139535323 true] [17592186343730 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =7+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{3}{7})=(-25.376\\,933…)^{∘}≈-{25.377}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{25.377}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={334.623}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSo,  our first solution is ${x}_{1}={334.623}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={25.377}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={25.377}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/assets/2358d2c829f52ba8727afc10a609f923ca441bb55dc398cda78c619454f6eac5.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{25.377}^{∘} \\\\  & ={205.377}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈{205}^{∘},\\,x≈{335}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343732 13194139535323 true] [17592186343731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343733 13194139535323 true] [17592186343731 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535323 true] [17592186343731 1041 "field-1" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343731 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343732 13194139535323 true] [17592186343731 1110 #uuid "deb06272-2dd7-53c0-a9ac-40dfef3ec089" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343732 1034 "205" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535323 true] [17592186343732 1111 #uuid "d5de5934-d762-554e-9bc6-54960f23fa75" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343733 1034 "25" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535323 true] [17592186343733 1111 #uuid "b9a344ae-c1a6-5f5f-a096-a66d926f1d2c" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343734 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343735 13194139535323 true] [17592186343734 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535323 true] [17592186343734 1041 "field-2" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343734 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343735 13194139535323 true] [17592186343734 1110 #uuid "712f34e8-a73a-51dc-8e5e-7f215f9c90ce" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343735 1034 "335" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535323 true] [17592186343735 1111 #uuid "737ee07b-e384-58c6-b1e3-24519c6cc192" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343736 1017 #edb/ref 17592186343737 13194139535323 true] [17592186343736 1089 "q-342050" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343736 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535323 true] [17592186343736 1100 "Given a curve $x=-\\frac{5}{y}+{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-4,1)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343736 1113 #uuid "4c4511dd-c475-5538-9512-79a65c337158" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343736 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{5}{y}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-5{y}^{-1}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-5(-{y}^{-2})+2y \\\\  & =2y+5{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =2y+\\frac{5}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{3}+5}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{3}+5}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-4,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-4,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2(1)^{3}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (x-(-4)) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{7}x+\\frac{4}{7}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{7}x+\\frac{11}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343738 13194139535323 true] [17592186343737 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535323 true] [17592186343737 1041 "field-1" 13194139535323 true] [17592186343737 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343738 131941395